    "body":  "## Context\n\nOGC-782 M4 introduces the canonical Microbiology WHONET Configure → Preview → Generate flow and removes the competing Reports menu entry. The older `ExportWHONETReportByDate` implementation remains in the codebase because its direct callers and compatibility obligations have not yet been audited.\n\nThis issue tracks the required legacy-path cleanup under Constitution Principle X. It is intentionally outside the M4 manual-export acceptance boundary.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Inventory all direct callers, routes, permissions, and report-menu dependencies of the legacy WHONET action.\n- Confirm whether any supported deployment still depends on the old entry point.\n- Migrate supported callers to the canonical microbiology export service/route or document a product-approved compatibility boundary.\n- Remove the legacy action and duplicated orchestration once no supported caller remains.\n- Retain one authoritative CSV renderer/service path; do not introduce dual-write or a second exporter.\n- Add focused regression coverage for the retained path and prove the legacy route is unavailable after removal.\n- Update the OGC-782 engineering crosswalk and M4 follow-up status.\n\n## Related\n\n- OGC-782 M4 branch: `feat/782-ogc-782-microbiology-m10-whonet-export`\n- Jira: OGC-794\n- Spec: `specs/782-ogc-782-microbiology-m10-whonet-export/`",
